          "recorded_role": "tool_result",
          "role": "tool_result",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "653\t\n654\t\\subsection{Extended Training Dynamics}\\label{sec:extended_training}\n655\t\n656\tOne Walker seed (s3, exp\\_045) was extended from 112K to approximately 302K steps to investigate long-horizon CIVO dynamics. After onset (NVE peak $4.91\\times$ at 132K steps), the system exhibited complete self-recovery: NVE declined to $0.05\\times$ and evaluation performance recovered to 867.6 (94.7\\% of baseline). This recovery required approximately 190K additional training steps beyond onset. The trajectory shows a single onset--recovery cycle with no recurrence, suggesting that the CIVO feedback loop can break spontaneously given sufficient training---though at substantial computational cost that the frozen $\\dt$-embedding diagnostic eliminates entirely.\n657\t\n658\t\\subsection{Why MPC Is Immune}"
            }
          ],
          "metadata": {
            "session": "worker_paper_190k_post_onset_fix_20260524T083102",
            "tool": "Read",
            "elapsed_ms": 0
          },
          "id": "event-000024"
