          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "654\t\n655\tOne Walker seed (s3, exp\\_045) was extended from 112K to approximately 302K steps to investigate long-horizon CIVO dynamics. After onset (NVE peak $4.91\\times$ at 132K steps), the system exhibited complete self-recovery: NVE declined to $0.05\\times$ and evaluation performance recovered to 867.6 (94.7\\% of baseline). This recovery required approximately 190K additional training steps beyond onset. The trajectory shows a single onset--recovery cycle with no recurrence, suggesting that the CIVO feedback loop can break spontaneously given sufficient training---though at substantial computational cost that the frozen $\\dt$-embedding diagnostic eliminates entirely.\n656\t\n657\t\\subsection{Why MPC Is Immune}\n658\t\\label{sec:mpc_immune}"
            }
          ],
